Z||000007||CJ||07-10-2001||10:02 AM||||I don't know if my 88 GT with the V6 is OBD I or OBD II, but I do know that you can read the codes without a scanner.  <P>To read the codes, ground the diagnostic terminal of the ALDL connector located under the center console.  The "Service Engine Soon" light will flash Code 12 three times and then flash each code stored in memory three times.  All codes stored in memory would have been read when Code 12 was flashed again.  No new codes can be stored when in the Diagnositics Mode (diagnostics lead grounded.)  This eliminates confusion while the system is being worked on.<P>To clear the codes from memory:<BR>   Ignition "OFF"<BR>   Disconnect 12 volt pigtail connector <BR>     located near the battery.<P>The diagnositic terminal is terminal "B" on the ALDL connector, and terminal "A" is grounded.  Looking at the connector, Terminal "A" is the furthest to the right, on the top row, and "B" is next to it.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000008||00lE||07-10-2001||01:02 PM||||Why not switch it out to an older PCM such as the 1227730 or 1227727 from a pre-94 3.1 MPFI?  They are OBD-I and will run that engine just fine, although not in sequential fuel injection (SFI) mode.  Unless your into gas milleage numbers, the SFI should not be an important factor anyway.  The switch to a OBD-I PCM like those mentioned above will allow custom chip programming to achieve much better performance, something that is not likely to happen with the OBD-II encrypted data system, unless you own or work at a GM dealership service shop that is.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||lowCG||07-10-2001||08:00 PM||||I've got a funky Actron scanner($120) that does just that,has been helpful indeed with my OBDII swap,but I haven't done any tuning,which requires some expensive software,laptop and a $nap-On scanner.<BR>I make do with an air/fuel controller instead.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||07-10-2001||08:11 PM||||OBD II sucks.<P>I junked my 3400 series computer...if anyone wants it you can have it(if I can find it). <BR>Lets see...top speed of whatever the original tires are rated for...so for my 97 Silouette van---85mph.<P>Also a nice feature...documented in the manual...ABUSE MANAGEMENT CONTROL.  If you were going to take the car to the dealer, they would know if you "beat" on your car!<P>Joe<BR>3400 series 300hp<BR>TEC-II Engine control System||||reg||1
